    "text": "Se \u00e6lmihtiga Wealdend, \u00f0e ne ongann n\u00e6fre, & se \u00f0e ana is so\u00f0 God, gesceop ealle \u00f0ing, gesewenlice &\nSe is so\u00f0lice lufu \u00f0\u00e6s so\u00f0f\u00e6stan F\u00e6der, & his Suna lufu, & heora begra willa, for \u00f0an \u00f0e hi wylla\u00f0 an.\n& \u00f0urh \u00f0one Gast syndon so\u00f0lice geliff\u00e6ste ealle \u00f0a gesceafta \u00f0e se F\u00e6der gesceop \u00feurh his\n\u00d0eos is seo halige \u00f0rynnyss \u00fee ealle \u00feing gesceop, an anre Godcundnysse \u00e6fre wuniende, on anum\nEnglas he gesceop on \u00e6nlicre f\u00e6gernysse, manega \u00f0usenda, on micelre streng\u00f0e, \u00fe\u00e6t hi mihton geseon\nHi nabba\u00f0 nanne lichaman, ac hi libba\u00f0 on gaste, ungesewenlice us \u00fee on synnum libba\u00f0.\nAnd \u00fea halgan englas, \u00fee on heofenum wunia\u00f0, ne worhton n\u00e6fre nane synne, ne hi syngian ne magon,\nAnd hi wurdon \u00f0a awende to awyrgedum deoflum, for \u00f0an \u00f0e hi noldon habban heora Scyppend heom\n\u00d0a ne mihte he gewunian on \u00f0\u00e6re micclan m\u00e6r\u00f0e, ne eac his gegadan butan Godes mihte, ac wurdon\nAnd \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6ra yfela \u00f0e on \u00f0issere worulde becym\u00f0, eall hit gewyr\u00f0 \u00e6fre \u00feurh \u00fea awyrgedan gastas, &\nWitodlice on angynne se \u00e6lmihtiga God ealle \u00f0ing gesceop, heofonas & eor\u00f0an, & ealne middaneard,\nAc se mildheorta F\u00e6der, \u00f0e us to mannum gesceop \u00feurh his ancennedan Suna, wolde eft alysan \u00f0urh\n\u00d0a on \u00fe\u00e6re syxtan ylde \u00feyssere worulde asende se halga F\u00e6der his heahengel Gabriel to Marian \u00feam\nHeo wear\u00f0 \u00f0a mid cilde \u00e6fter \u00fe\u00e6re segene, & heo eode mid \u00feam cilde \u00e6fter gewunan nigon mon\u00f0as\n\u00d0onne we wyr\u00f0ia\u00f0 on Middewintres D\u00e6ge ures H\u00e6lendes acennednysse, hu he to mannum com on\nTwelf dagas we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 to wyr\u00f0mynte \u00feam H\u00e6lende mid urum lofsangum for his micclan lufe on his\nOn \u00f0am twelftan d\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6re tide ymbganges we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid lofsangum hu \u00f0a geleaffullan cyningas of\nOn \u00f0am feowerteogo\u00f0an d\u00e6ge fram his acennednysse, \u00fee we cwe\u00f0a\u00f0 on Englisc Candelm\u00e6ssed\u00e6g, b\u00e6r\nHe worhte on \u00f0issere worulde wundra wel fela, to geswutelienne \u00fe\u00e6t he so\u00f0 God is: blinde he geh\u00e6lde\nUppan sae he eode, & \u00fea s\u00e6lican y\u00f0a hine ab\u00e6ron; & he \u00feone blawendan wind mid his h\u00e6se gestilde,\nW\u00e6ter he awende to wynsuman wine, & ealle untrumnyssa he ea\u00f0elice geh\u00e6lde, & \u00f0a deadan ar\u00e6rde\nOn sumne s\u00e6l he afedde fif \u00feusend manna, butan wifum & cildum, & hi wel gereordode, mid fif\nOn o\u00f0rum s\u00e6le he afedde feower \u00f0usend manna mid seofon hlafum & feawum fixum, & hi l\u00e6fdon\n\u00d0yllice wundra wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 hine.\nOn Lenctenes anginne we eac swylce wyr\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid urum lofsangum hu se leofa H\u00e6lend on \u00f0am\nEft we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 on ufeweardan Lenctene on halgum r\u00e6dingum \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes \u00f0rowunge, hu he us\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea bebyrged on \u00f0am ylcan d\u00e6ge, & he aras of dea\u00f0e on \u00f0am \u00feriddan d\u00e6ge, mid \u00f0am ylcan\nAnd we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 \u00fea tid wur\u00f0lice mid sangum seofon niht on an, swylce hit an d\u00e6g sy, for \u00f0\u00e6re\nOn \u00f0am feowerteoge\u00f0an d\u00e6ge \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e he of dea\u00f0e aras he astah to heofonum to his halgan F\u00e6der,\nAnd we eac wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 wur\u00f0lice \u00f0one d\u00e6g on \u00fe\u00e6re Gangwucan, for \u00f0an \u00fee he geopenode us on \u00f0am\nAnd he sitt nu on heofonum so\u00felice an Crist \u00e6t his F\u00e6der swi\u00f0ran, & ealra gesceafta gewylt, & cym\u00f0\nEft \u00f0\u00e6s embe tyn niht on urum \u00f0eowdome we m\u00e6rsia\u00f0 \u00feone d\u00e6g mid m\u00e6rlicum wyr\u00f0mynte \u00fee we\n& hi eac gebylde to \u00f0\u00e6re godspellican bodunge, swa \u00fe\u00e6t hi unforhte ferdon geond \u00feas woruld, & \u00fea\nSeofon dagas we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 mid urum lofsange on cyrcan \u00feone halgan tocyme \u00fe\u00e6s Halgan Gastes, for\nHe tod\u00e6l\u00f0 his gifa on geleaffullum mannum be \u00f0am \u00f0e he sylf wyle, for \u00f0an \u00f0e he so\u00f0 God is.\nOn \u00f0\u00e6re Pentecosten wucan we wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 \u00fea tid, & on \u00f0am Sunnand\u00e6ge \u00f0e sy\u00f0\u00f0an bi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r\u00e6fter we\nWe secga\u00f0 nu be \u00f0am so\u00f0an Gode \u00fee ealle \u00f0ing gesceop, se \u00f0e ana is God, \u00fe\u00e6t he is wunigende, swa\nSe \u00e6lmihtiga F\u00e6der nis of nanum o\u00f0rum; se gestrynde \u00e6nne Sunu of him anum acennedne, & se w\u00e6s\nHe nis na acenned, ac he cym\u00f0 of him bam swa swa lufu & willa, for \u00f0an \u00fee hi wylla\u00f0 an, se F\u00e6der &\nHi synd \u00fery on namum on \u00f0rynnysse wunigende, ac seo an Godcundnyss \u00fee him eallum is gem\u00e6ne\nNu is se F\u00e6der F\u00e6der & se Suna Sunu, & heora begra Willa, \u00fe\u00e6t is witodlice seo Lufu heora micclan\nSe Sunu ana is so\u00f0lice acenned \u00e6rest of \u00feam F\u00e6der buton \u00e6lcere meder, & eft of Marian butan\n\u00d0\u00e6s we him \u00f0ancia\u00f0 on urum \u00feeowdome, & his halgan F\u00e6der \u00fee hine asende to us, \u00feam is an",
